<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Boot's console logging, with one change: the password of a URL (scheme://user:password@host) is
masked on every line, message and stack trace alike.

Why: when a server answers an error, WebClient writes the full request URL, userinfo included, into
the exception's message ("500 Internal Server Error from GET http://user:password@host/...") and
into the "Request to GET ..." checkpoint of its stack trace. With the cause now kept on
TechnicalException, those traces reach the ERROR log. No URL here is meant to carry credentials
(wely-users' reader secret travels in a header, MongoDB's URI is never logged), so this is a safety
net for a mistyped USERS_API_URL, not a feature.

The whole Boot pattern is wrapped in %replace, then %nopex stops logback from appending a second,
unmasked stack trace of its own.
-->
<configuration>
	<include resource="org/springframework/boot/logging/logback/defaults.xml"/>

	<property name="CONSOLE_LOG_PATTERN"
			  value="%replace(${CONSOLE_LOG_PATTERN}){'(://[^/\s:@]+:)[^/\s@]+@', '$1****@'}%nopex"/>

	<include resource="org/springframework/boot/logging/logback/console-appender.xml"/>

	<root level="INFO">
		<appender-ref ref="CONSOLE"/>
	</root>
</configuration>
